    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94191" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῑμόω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιμός</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn up the nose</i>, and
			metaph.,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέμφομαι</span> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally, <i>bend
				upwards</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἰγνύαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν αὐχένα, τὰ νῶτα</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				1.12
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>become</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιμός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				35
			</span></i>; of the nose, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				6.1.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόδες σεσιμωμένοι</span>
			<i>upturned</i> feet, as of some wading birds, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				693a7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				60
			</span></i>.</div>
